   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Vaccine program implementation capacity strengthened 
Indicator: 196 mobile teams deployed to administer vaccines to the population in remote and rural areas, including all women 
Achievement: 4290 
Progress/Status: Over-achieved:
 
The number of mobile teams mobilized were:  4,290; the number of workers in the team is 12,870, 85.8% of which or 11,054 were women and 14.2% or 1,816 were men. 
Data Source: Periodic progress reports prepared by the MOHSPP</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2020"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="196"></target>
     <actual value="4290"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Vaccine program implementation capacity strengthened 
Indicator: At least 50% of the population reached by COVID-19 information campaigns that include gender concerns.

Examples of gender concerns are women&amp;apos;s access to scientific information and real-time updates on the vaccines&amp;apos; safety and efficacy, and gender-sensitive administration of vaccines, especially to women, among others. 
Achievement: 50 
Progress/Status: Over-achieved:

A video on Immunization for the Population was released in national and local television networks nationwide, reaching more than 50% of the population. Campaign materials (nearly 68,650 booklets and posters) have been distributed nationwide, 80% of which were targeted for women.
More targeted campaigns were undertaken to over 3,000 representatives (81% female) of mahallas, committees, mass media, medical workers, teachers, community leaders, local police officers, religious clergy; and housewives. 
Data Source: Satisfaction survey for vaccine recipients and social media analytics</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2020"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="50"></target>
     <actual value="50"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Vaccine program implementation capacity strengthened 
Indicator: At least 80% of vaccinated women and men find the vaccination services and post-vaccination information satisfactory, including the respectful and positive way their concerns are dealt with 
Achievement: 85 
Progress/Status: Over-achieved:

Around 85% of survey respondents indicated satisfaction of the vaccination process.  By gender, the rate is 86% for men and 84.5% for women. 

The total number of vaccinated populations is 3,487,503), including 1,693,760 men, which is 48.57% and 1,793,743 women which is 51.43%. 
Data Source: Satisfaction survey for vaccine recipients and social media analytics</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2020"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="80"></target>
     <actual value="85"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: COVID-19 vaccines procured and delivered to designated delivery points 
Indicator: At least 3.36 million doses (2 per person) of
COVID-19 vaccine (with syringes and safety boxes) delivered to designated delivery points 
Achievement: 3508800 
Progress/Status: Over-achieved:
 
3.508 million doses of Sinovac vaccines delivered by December 2021

The vaccines were delivered in two batches in 2021: on 6 December (546,000 doses expiring in September 2022) and 23 December (2,962,800 doses expiring in October 2022). Syringes were partially (1M) delivered in March 2022 with the remaining (2.859M) in June 2022. Safety boxes were likewise partially (10,000 pieces) delivered in March 2022 with the rest (38,600 pieces) in May 2022. 
Data Source: Periodic progress
reports prepared by the
MOHSPP, WHO, and
UNICEF</narrative>
    </description>
