   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Outcome</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Priority populations vaccinated against COVID-19</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">About 1.43 million people (1,428,571) in priority groups, based on the NDVP, vaccinated (data disaggregated by sex) 
Achievement: 1743751 
Progress/Status: Over-achieved.

3,487,503 vaccines or 99.48% of the delivered vaccines have been administered to individuals equivalent to a wastage rate of only 0.6%. 

Of the total vaccinated individuals, 51.43% were females and 48.57% were males. 

Assuming 2 doses per person, as earlier envisaged in the project, a total of 1,743,751 vaccinees received the complete dosage. 
Data Source: Periodic progress reports prepared by the MOHSPP, WHO, and UNICEF</narrative>
    </description>
